From 0aee0e822e5bd3323719f71f3c93b8599cecdb58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 17:32:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add multi-site row splitting, CC year/duration fields, and
 stage-4 geolocation scaffold

- enumerate_experimental_units() can now vary location/tillage/fertilize/
  herbicide/irrigation/soil/coordinates per unit (SITE_VARIABLE_FIELDS),
  so a paper with physically distinct sites under different management
  produces one row per site instead of blending their practices together
- Add cc_years_practiced (per-unit list of calendar years CC was
  practiced) and computed cc_duration_years (count of distinct years)
- Fix assemble_row() clobbering paper_id back to None even when
  PaperSpec.paper_id / --paper-id was set (paper_id is a schema field but
  never comes from all_fields)
- Add src/geolocation.py: point -> polygon resolution for the ground-
  truth workflow's Stage 4 (station registry match -> USDA CSB
  point-in-polygon -> tier D manual-NAIP-review queue), pure
  shapely/plain-dict matching logic with geopandas/fiona only at the
  station registry / CSB gdb loading boundary
- Add missing tests/test_pipeline.py, src/llm_client.py, and
  workflows/run_extraction.py from prior uncommitted work, plus new
  tests/test_geolocation.py (9 tests) and additional test_pipeline.py
  coverage for the site-splitting and cc_duration changes (39 tests total)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013MnfbuaTyFx97zerx93SFH
